  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "If the graphs of \\(2y+x+3=0\\) and \\(3y+ax+2=0\\) are to meet at right angles, the value of \\(a\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\pm\\dfrac23\\)",
    "B": "\\(-\\dfrac23\\)",
    "C": "\\(-\\dfrac32\\)",
    "D": "\\(6\\)",
    "E": "\\(-6\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "The coefficients of \\(y\\) are \\(2\\) and \\(3\\), so neither line is vertical, regardless of \\(a\\). Solving each equation for \\(y\\) reveals its slope:\n\\[\ny=-\\frac12x-\\frac32,\n\\qquad y=-\\frac a3x-\\frac23.\n\\]\nTwo lines with finite slopes are perpendicular exactly when the product of their slopes is \\(-1\\). Therefore\n\\[\n\\left(-\\frac12\\right)\\left(-\\frac a3\\right)=-1,\n\\qquad \\frac a6=-1,\n\\qquad a=-6.\n\\]\nAt this value the slopes are \\(-1/2\\) and \\(2\\), which are negative reciprocals and are distinct, so the lines meet at right angles. Thus \\(\\boxed{a=-6}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
